{"task_id": "HumanEval/25", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef factorize(n: int) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Return a list of prime factors for a given integer n.\n    The list elements are in non-decreasing order, and their product equals n.\n    \"\"\"\n    factors = []\n\n    if n <= 1:\n        return factors\n\n    # Handle factor 2\n    while n % 2 == 0:\n        factors.append(2)\n        n //= 2\n\n    # Handle odd factors\n    i = 3\n    while i * i <= n:\n        while n % i == 0:\n            factors.append(i)\n            n //= i\n        i += 2\n\n    # If n is still greater than 1, it must be a prime factor itself\n    if n > 1:\n        factors.append(n)\n\n    return factors"}
