{"task_id": "HumanEval/37", "solution": "def sort_even(l: list):\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a list l' where l' is identical to l at odd indices.\n    Its values at even indices are sorted versions of l's even-indexed values.\n    >>> sort_even([1, 2, 3])\n    [1, 2, 3]\n    >>> sort_even([5, 6, 3, 4])\n    [3, 6, 5, 4]\n    \"\"\"\n    output_list = list(l)\n\n    even_elements = []\n    for i in range(len(l)):\n        if i % 2 == 0:\n            even_elements.append(l[i])\n\n    even_elements.sort()\n\n    even_idx_counter = 0\n    for i in range(len(output_list)):\n        if i % 2 == 0:\n            output_list[i] = even_elements[even_idx_counter]\n            even_idx_counter += 1\n\n    return output_list"}
