{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"The Fib4 number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fib4(0) -> 0\n    fib4(1) -> 0\n    fib4(2) -> 2\n    fib4(3) -> 0\n    fib4(n) -> fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4).\n    Please write a function to efficiently compute the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence.  Do not use recursion.\n    >>> fib4(5)\n    4\n    >>> fib4(6)\n    8\n    >>> fib4(7)\n    14\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize the four most recent Fib4 numbers, starting with fib4(0) to fib4(3)\n    # These represent (fib4(i-4), fib4(i-3), fib4(i-2), fib4(i-1)) for the next iteration\n    a, b, c, d = 0, 0, 2, 0\n\n    # Iterate from the 4th term up to n, calculating each term iteratively\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_val = a + b + c + d\n        # Shift the window of values\n        a = b\n        b = c\n        c = d\n        d = next_val\n\n    return d"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "_fib_cache = [0, 0, 2, 0]\ndef fib4(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"The Fib4 number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fib4(0) -> 0\n    fib4(1) -> 0\n    fib4(2) -> 2\n    fib4(3) -> 0\n    fib4(n) -> fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4).\n    Please write a function to efficiently compute the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence.  Do not use recursion.\n    >>> fib4(5)\n    4\n    >>> fib4(6)\n    8\n    >>> fib4(7)\n    14\n    \"\"\"\n    # If n is already in the cache, return the stored value.\n    if n < len(_fib_cache):\n        return _fib_cache[n]\n\n    # Iteratively compute and store Fib4 numbers up to n.\n    for i in range(len(_fib_cache), n + 1):\n        next_fib = _fib_cache[i-1] + _fib_cache[i-2] + _fib_cache[i-3] + _fib_cache[i-4]\n        _fib_cache.append(next_fib)\n\n    return _fib_cache[n]"}
