{"task_id": "HumanEval/136", "solution": "def largest_smallest_integers(lst):\n    '''\n    Finds the largest negative and smallest positive integers in a list.\n    Returns (largest_negative, smallest_positive), using None if not found.\n    '''\n    largest_negative = None\n    smallest_positive = None\n\n    for number in lst:\n        if number < 0:\n            if largest_negative is None or number > largest_negative:\n                largest_negative = number\n        elif number > 0:\n            if smallest_positive is None or number < smallest_positive:\n                smallest_positive = number\n\n    return (largest_negative, smallest_positive)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/135", "solution": "def can_arrange(arr):\n    \"\"\"Identifies the largest index i where arr[i] < arr[i-1].\n    Returns i if found, otherwise -1.\"\"\"\n    # Iterate from the second-to-last element down to the second element.\n    # The range ensures arr[i-1] is always a valid index.\n    for i in range(len(arr) - 1, 0, -1):\n        # Check if the current element is strictly less than its predecessor.\n        if arr[i] < arr[i-1]:\n            # If true, this is the largest such index due to right-to-left iteration.\n            return i\n    # If the loop completes, no such index was found.\n    return -1"}
