{"task_id": "HumanEval/137", "solution": "from typing import Any, Union\nclass _InputValue:\n    \"\"\"\n    Encapsulates an input value, its original type, and a standardized float representation.\n    Handles string parsing for comma or period decimal separators.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, value: Any):\n        self._raw_value: Any = value\n        self._original_type: type = type(value)\n\n        # Determine numeric representation, handling string formats for conversion.\n        try:\n            self._numeric_representation: float = float(value)\n        except ValueError:\n            # If direct float conversion fails, it's likely a string with a comma.\n            self._numeric_representation = self._parse_string(value)\n\n    def get_raw_value(self) -> Any:\n        \"\"\"Returns the original input value.\"\"\"\n        return self._raw_value\n\n    def get_original_type(self) -> type:\n        \"\"\"Returns the original type of the input value.\"\"\"\n        return self._original_type\n\n    def get_numeric_representation(self) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Returns the numeric (float) representation of the input value.\"\"\"\n        return self._numeric_representation\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _parse_string(input_str: str) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Converts string inputs to floats, specifically handling '.' and ',' as decimal separators.\"\"\"\n        # Replace comma with period to enable standard float conversion.\n        parsed_str = input_str.replace(',', '.')\n        return float(parsed_str)\ndef compare_one(a: Union[int, float, str], b: Union[int, float, str]) -> Union[int, float, str, None]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compares two real numbers (int, float, or string) and returns the numerically larger value\n    in its original type, or None if they are equal.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Create _InputValue instances to normalize inputs for comparison.\n    input_a = _InputValue(a)\n    input_b = _InputValue(b)\n\n    # Retrieve numeric representations for direct comparison.\n    num_a = input_a.get_numeric_representation()\n    num_b = input_b.get_numeric_representation()\n\n    # Compare values and return the raw value of the larger one, or None if equal.\n    if num_a == num_b:\n        return None\n    elif num_a > num_b:\n        return input_a.get_raw_value()\n    else: # num_b > num_a\n        return input_b.get_raw_value()"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/128", "solution": "def prod_signs(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of magnitudes multiplied by the product of signs (1, -1, or 0) for integers in an array.\n    Returns None if the input array is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return None\n\n    sum_magnitudes = 0\n    product_signs = 1\n\n    for number in arr:\n        sum_magnitudes += abs(number)\n\n        current_sign = 0\n        if number > 0:\n            current_sign = 1\n        elif number < 0:\n            current_sign = -1\n        # If number == 0, current_sign remains 0.\n\n        product_signs *= current_sign\n\n    return sum_magnitudes * product_signs"}
